    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47645" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤτριον</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτριον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>warp</i> (the woof
			being <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρόκη</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				268a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				18.33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.288
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>, pl.): in pl., <i>a thin, fine cloth</i>, such that one
			could see between the threads, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤτρια πέπλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					1421
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤτρια βύβλων</span>
			<i>leaves made of strips of</i> papyrus, prob. cj. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.350
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ διὰ ἠτρίου ἠθημένον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					19.98
				</span></i>
			.</div>
